1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
This robot has no pinky.

2
00:00:01,981 --> 00:00:03,010
On purpose.

3
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:04,833
Boston Dynamics says its engineers

4
00:00:04,838 --> 00:00:06,133
taped their ring and pinky

5
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:07,633
fingers together for a day.

6
00:00:07,695 --> 00:00:08,333
The verdict?

7
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:09,433
Leave it out.

8
00:00:09,486 --> 00:00:11,533
Atlas’s new hand has four digits,

9
00:00:11,543 --> 00:00:12,167
but thirteen

10
00:00:12,152 --> 00:00:13,267
degrees of freedom.

11
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:14,867
Independent ways to move.

12
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:16,567
The company says it can pinch,

13
00:00:16,571 --> 00:00:17,333
turn objects,

14
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:18,667
and press tool triggers.

15
00:00:18,743 --> 00:00:19,900
A fifth digit would mean

16
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:21,371
three more actuators.

17
00:00:21,371 --> 00:00:22,286
More cost.

18
00:00:22,286 --> 00:00:23,200
More bulk.

19
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,133
More things to break.

20
00:00:24,324 --> 00:00:25,933
So the goal is a useful,

21
00:00:25,924 --> 00:00:27,181
reliable hand.

22
00:00:27,181 --> 00:00:28,500
Looking human is optional.

23
00:00:28,781 --> 00:00:30,200
Apparently, even robots

24
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:31,067
have a budget.
